Month = {FEB},
Abstract = {Recently, authentication technologies integrated with the Internet of
   Things (IoT) and cloud computing have been promptly investigated for
   secure data retrieval and robust access control on large-scale IoT
   networks. However, it does not have a best practice for simultaneously
   deploying IoT and cloud computing with robust security. In this study,
   we present a novel authentication scheme for IoT-based architectures
   combined with cloud servers. To pursue the best efficiency, lightweight
   crypto-modules, such as one-way hash function and exclusive-or
   operation, are adopted in our authentication scheme. It not only removes
   the computation burden but also makes our proposed scheme suitable for
   resource-limited objects, such as sensors or IoT devices. Through the
   formal verification delivered by Proverif, the security robustness of
   the proposed authentication scheme is guaranteed. Furthermore, the
   performance evaluation presents the practicability of our proposed
   scheme in which a user-acceptable computation cost is achieved. (C) 2018
   Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.},
