Note = {1st International Conference on Emerging Trends in Information
   Technology (ICETIT), Inst Informat Technol \& Management, New Delhi,
   INDIA, JUN 21-22, 2019},
Abstract = {Advances in Information Technology field have replaced local storage of
   data with cloud storage which has become the crux of the day. As the
   number of people adopting storage as a service is increasing, security
   of personal and private information stored on cloud remains a major
   concern. Different approaches to achieve security have been used like
   encryption, file division, access control security (ACS),
   authentication, authorization and many more.
   We demonstrate `Enigma': A hybrid approach to file security in cloud
   that outdoes all these traditional methods and provides unmatched
   security. In our approach, we introduce the concept of `jigsaw division'
   which not only enhances division approach but also allows us to employ
   selective encryption thus combining best of both worlds. We show that
   our strategy provides better security and at the same time minimally
   hampers the retrieval time. We model our system using graph and
   demonstrate the use of vertex coloring algorithm for distributing file
   fragments across different nodes. By doing this we aim to turn the act
   of hacking and retrieving meaningful information into a puzzle for all
   the Black Hats out there!},
