   Development (INDIACom), Bharati Vidyapeeth, New Delhi, INDIA, MAR 13-15,
   2019},
Abstract = {Cloud computing proved to be the most useful computing paradigm in
   today's world. Not only has it allowed enterprises to process and store
   their business logic or data economically viable and computationally
   feasible, but it has also helped in enhancing their product security and
   in creating a centralized repository. But cloud computing faces a very
   serious issue i.e. it is located far away from the data generating
   devices or system which could allow data modification or loss. Fog
   computing was introduced due to the very reason. Even though the term is
   new, but a lot of research is ongoing which proves its need and
   viability. In this paper, we will give a brief introduction followed by
   the Fog computing needs, its usage scenarios, its applications and then
   security issues related to fog will be discussed. At last, our
   contribution in this paper, some of the recent research works in fog
   security, comparison of surveys focusing on security algorithms and
   distributed architecture will be mentioned and then summed up with a
   conclusion.},
