Note = {9th International Congress on Information and Communication Technology
   (ICICT), London, ENGLAND, FEB 19-22, 2024},
Abstract = {Navigating the complex realm of secure cloud storage, our application
   offers a uniquely robust and user-friendly data storage solution,
   adeptly bridging AES-256 encryption and public key searchable encryption
   to safeguard user data while maintaining accessible retrieval.
   Specifically, the Searchable Encryption sub-module leverages the
   unaltered scheme proposed by Senouci et al. In J Syst Archit 119:102271
   {[}1], foundational in enabling secure, efficient data searchability
   without necessitating decryption. Furthermore, detailed access control
   and comprehensive audit logging empower users with precise control and
   transparent oversight of their stored data, enhancing data security and
   user trust. With an architecture that synergizes stringent security
   protocols and user-centric design, the application presents a paradigm
   shift in secure cloud storage, achieving a harmonious balance between
   impenetrable data security and user accessibility, thereby setting a new
   benchmark in secure data storage and retrieval in cloud environments.},
