   Blanca, ARGENTINA, AUG 12-16, 2024},
Abstract = {This study proposes a framework that leverages ML algorithms for the
   cybersecurity of telemedicine systems in the Department of Cordoba,
   Colombia, addressing challenges amplified by the COVID-19 pandemic. The
   framework emphasizes enhancing the processing capabilities and
   reliability in managing clinical information, particularly focusing on
   the RES. It integrates a PGaaS aligned with the OWASP guidelines, aiming
   to neutralize emerging threats using advanced IA models. The system
   incorporates data encryption, 2FA-based Access Control, continuous
   backups, code obfuscation, and watermarking, all supported by a suitable
   legal framework. These components are combined into a comprehensive
   monitoring and auditing scheme to ensure robust protection against
   intelligent intrusions and the compromise of medical data.},
